ADDENDA <Act No. 18303, Jul. 20, 2021>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 6 months after its promulgation.
Article 2 (Preparations for enforcement of this Act)
Any preparatory act for the enforcement of this Act, such as the appointment or commissioning of members and staff members of the Committee and the Working Committee engaged in activities for discovering the truth and preparation for the establishment of the Committee and the Working Committee in accordance with the enforcement of this Act, may be performed before this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to commencement of terms of office of commissioners)
The term of office of the first members commissioned in accordance with this Act shall be deemed to begin on the date this Act enters into force.
Article 4 (Transitional measures regarding investigation for discovering truth on Yeosu-Suncheon October 19 Incident)
Where a reporter files for a reinvestigation into the Yeosu-Suncheon October 19 Incident, from among cases received by the Truth and Reconciliation Commission under the Framework Act on Settling the Past for Truth and Reconciliation (Act No. 7542), in which the investigation for discovering the truth has not been completed or has been insufficient due to limitation of the investigation period, and if the Committee deems it necessary for additional investigations for discovering the truth, it may decide to commence a fact-finding investigation in accordance with Article 7(1).

